{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1328519-aberrant-mega-cunning-and-initiative","id":1328519,"title":"[Aberrant] Mega-Cunning and Initiative","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-07-31T07:37:28-07:00","id":1328519,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [Aberrant] Mega-Cunning and Initiative","content":"Hmm, so Mega-Cunning increases your speed scale for the purposes of Initiative. That is cool. However, since Scale is a function of your ability relative to others, how does this apply to Initiative?<br /> <br /> If you are fighting one Nova with a Speed Scale for Initiative of 1 and another with 3, and you have 2. When you roll for Initiative, you apply +2 Enhancement per difference in Speed Scale. This means you have one Tick Count number for one opponent and a different Tick Count number for another. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2018-bioagent","name":"Bioagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T07:41:36-07:00","id":1328520,"title":"","content":"Simple solution is just treat Initiative as a scale one contest and all Novas add their appropriate Enhancement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-31T07:42:19-07:00","id":1328521,"title":"","content":"Just subtract the lowest scale from all the rolls. So, speed scale 1 would get +0 enhancements, speed scale 2 would get +2 enhancements, and speed scale 3 would get +4 enhancements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}